"\n"
"A button on manufacturing orders opens them in the barcode reading\n"
"screen of ``stock_barcodes``. Components, the product to manufacture and\n"
"byproducts are captured as ``mrp_capture`` does.\n"
"\n"
".. IMPORTANT::\n"
"   This is an alpha version, the data model and design can change at any "
"time without warning.\n"
"   Only for development or testing purpose, do not use in production.\n"
"   `More details on development status <https://odoo-community.org/page/"
"development-status>`_\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Open a confirmed manufacturing order and press *Scan*. Read the\n"
"components to consume, the product to manufacture (with its lot or\n"
"package) and the byproducts, then validate to mark the order as done.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/OCA/stock-logistics-"
"barcode/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been "
"reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and "
"welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/OCA/stock-logistics-barcode/issues/new?"
